rem Approximating a Sum
rem https://projecteuler.net/problem=756

use numbers
use sequences
use io
use cli

arg Size integer = 12345678
arg Picks integer = 12345

rem Point k adds f(k) times the gap
rem before it, so its expected share is
rem 1 - C(n-k, m) / C(n, m). Hence
rem E = sum of f(k) C(n-k, m) / C(n, m),
rem a prefix product of (n-m-i)/(n-i).
rem The ratio is below e^(-k m / n), so
rem a bounded prefix is enough.
Spread = Size // Picks
Reach = (Size - Picks) min (90 * Spread)
Idx = 1 to Reach
Down = Size - Picks - Idx + 1
Up = Size - Idx + 1
Ratio = Down / Up scan * with 1.0
Primes = primes to Reach copy
rem Totients by ragged prime multiples.
Count = Reach // Primes
Ends = Count scan +
Starts = Ends - Count
Total = Count sum
Marks = array shape Total fill 0
Marks Starts = 1
Owner = (Marks scan +) - 1
Run = 0 to Total - 1
Step = Run - Starts Owner + 1
Prime = Primes Owner
Spot = Step * Prime - 1
Top = array shape Reach fill 1
Bot = array shape Reach fill 1
Top Spot *= Prime - 1 .accumulate
Bot Spot *= Prime .accumulate
Phi = Idx // Bot * Top
Terms = Phi * (Ratio drop 1)
Answer = (Terms sum) round 6
Answer print
